Licences of files bundled in this package
=========================================

The sbom package itself is MIT licensed (see LICENSE). This file lists every
file under inst/ with its source, copyright, licence and changes. The schemas
are third-party, copied unmodified from upstream unless stated otherwise;
their exact sources, tags and checksums are in inst/schemas/MANIFEST.csv, and
data-raw/schemas.R reproduces them.

sbom does not bundle the ISO/IEC 19770-2:2015 (SWID) schema: ISO's notice
grants use of that schema for implementing the standard, not clearly its
redistribution. validate_sbom() checks a SWID tag against sbom's own
structural rules instead, or against the ISO schema itself when the option
sbom.swid_xsd names a copy of it exactly as ISO publishes it (checked by its
SHA-256). sbom bundles the two W3C schemas that the ISO schema imports, listed
below, so that this check needs no network.

