sbom's own files
----------------

The files below were written for this package, or generated by its data-raw/
scripts, and are MIT licensed like the rest of it, with the copyright holder
that LICENSE names.

inst/extdata/licenses.csv, inst/extdata/licenses.dcf
  The SPDX expression for each licence specification (the License field) in
  use on CRAN and Bioconductor, generated by data-raw/licenses.R; licenses.dcf
  records when and from what. The specifications are every distinct License
  value in tools::CRAN_package_db() and in the Bioconductor release VIEWS files
  (software, annotation, experiment and workflow packages), and R's own
  "GPL-2 | GPL-3". Each is mapped to SPDX by R's own licence analysis:
  tools:::analyze_license() and the SPDX identifiers in R's licence database
  (share/licenses/license.db, read with tools:::R_license_db()), which are
  part of R. Following R Observatory's rule, an expression is kept only when
  every alternative maps to SPDX, none is "file LICENSE" alone, and
  "+ file LICENSE" follows only a licence that R's database marks as
  extensible; otherwise the spdx column is empty. The deprecated id
  BSD-2-Clause-FreeBSD is replaced with BSD-2-Clause-Views. The file holds
  licence specifications and SPDX identifiers only, no licence text.

inst/extdata/javascript.csv
  sbom's rules for recognising JavaScript and CSS libraries that packages
  bundle, by file name and header; written for this package.

inst/extdata/vendored.csv
  sbom's rules for recognising C and C++ libraries that packages copy into
  their sources; written for this package.

inst/extdata/app.R, inst/extdata/manifest.json, inst/extdata/renv.lock
  Example inputs for the examples of sbom_rsconnect(), sbom_renv() and sbom(),
  written for this package. The packages they name are fictitious (ghpkg,
  ppmpkg, biocpkg, localpkg, with example.org addresses), except cli and glue,
  which are described by short excerpts of their CRAN package metadata (name,
  version, title, licence field, maintainer, URLs).

inst/schemas/MANIFEST.csv
  The source, tag, SHA-256 checksum and modification flag of each bundled
  schema, written by data-raw/schemas.R.

